      "sheet": null,
      "row_index": null,
      "page": null,
      "raw_text": "1 injection (1 month): MSAF score decreased significantly 2 injections (2 months): symptoms resolved. No relapse. 3 injections (3 months): MSAF score decreased from a baseline of 7–10/10 to 0/10. No relapse. During COVID‐19 quarantine, one dose was missed, and after 6 weeks the patient resumed being symptomatic and steroid‐dependent. When omalizumab was restarted, symptoms completely disappeared, and steroids were discontinued. Prior to omalizumab, no skin lesions suggestive of MPCM were able to be observed (began to regress at 5 years old)"
